    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.sessions\r\n\r\n### Question\r\n\r\nHi,\r\n\r\nI am using Neovim 0.12.1 (the one with `:restart` command available) and trying to use mini.sessions restart() - https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-sessions.html#minisessions.restart\r\n\r\nIn my config, I have declared this keymap:\r\n\r\n` vim.keymap.set('n', '<Leader>r', '<Cmd>lua MiniSessions.restart()<CR>', { desc = 'Restart neovim' })\r\n`\r\n\r\nWhen I try to use it, it throws error:\r\n\r\n```\r\nE5108: Lua: [string \":lua\"]:1: attempt to call field 'restart' (a nil value)\r\nstack traceback:\r\n        [string \":lua\"]:1: in main chunk\r\n```\r\n\r\nAPI doesn't take any argument and from this code: https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/69b7433355664cf76898eb86a12a019f39bd86d1/lua/mini/sessions.lua#L345\r\n\r\nlooks like it should work in all situation. If session is loaded it would restart same session, if session is not loaded, it creates temporary session and load it when neovim restarts.\r\n\r\nCan someone please tell me how to use this API?\r\n",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.sessions</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hi,</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I am using Neovim 0.12.1 (the one with <code class=\"notranslate\">:restart</code> command available) and trying to use mini.sessions restart() - <a href=\"https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-sessions.html#minisessions.restart\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-sessions.html#minisessions.restart</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In my config, I have declared this keymap:</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">vim.keymap.set('n', '&lt;Leader&gt;r', '&lt;Cmd&gt;lua MiniSessions.restart()&lt;CR&gt;', { desc = 'Restart neovim' })</code></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">When I try to use it, it throws error:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"E5108: Lua: [string &quot;:lua&quot;]:1: attempt to call field 'restart' (a nil value)\nstack traceback:\n        [string &quot;:lua&quot;]:1: in main chunk\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">E5108: Lua: [string \":lua\"]:1: attempt to call field 'restart' (a nil value)\nstack traceback:\n        [string \":lua\"]:1: in main chunk\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">API doesn't take any argument and from this code: </p><div class=\"Box Box--condensed my-2\">\n  <div class=\"Box-header f6\">\n    <p class=\"mb-0 text-bold\">\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/69b7433355664cf76898eb86a12a019f39bd86d1/lua/mini/sessions.lua#L345\">mini.nvim/lua/mini/sessions.lua</a>\n    </p>\n    <p class=\"mb-0 color-fg-muted\">\n         Line 345\n      in\n      <a data-pjax=\"true\" class=\"commit-tease-sha Link--inTextBlock\" href=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/commit/69b7433355664cf76898eb86a12a019f39bd86d1\">69b7433</a>\n    </p>\n  </div>\n  <div itemprop=\"text\" class=\"Box-body p-0 blob-wrapper blob-wrapper-embedded data\">\n    <table class=\"highlight tab-size mb-0 js-file-line-container\" data-tab-size=\"8\" data-paste-markdown-skip=\"\">\n\n        <tbody><tr class=\"border-0\">\n          <td id=\"L345\" class=\"blob-num border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default\" data-line-number=\"345\"></td>\n          <td id=\"LC345\" class=\"blob-code border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default blob-code-inner js-file-line\"> <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniSessions</span>.<span class=\"pl-en\">restart</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>() </td>\n        </tr>\n    </tbody></table>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<p></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">looks like it should work in all situation. If session is loaded it would restart same session, if session is not loaded, it creates temporary session and load it when neovim restarts.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Can someone please tell me how to use this API?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.sessions\nQuestion\nHi,\nI am using Neovim 0.12.1 (the one with :restart command available) and trying to use mini.sessions restart() - https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-sessions.html#minisessions.restart\nIn my config, I have declared this keymap:\nvim.keymap.set('n', '<Leader>r', '<Cmd>lua MiniSessions.restart()<CR>', { desc = 'Restart neovim' })\nWhen I try to use it, it throws error:\nE5108: Lua: [string \":lua\"]:1: attempt to call field 'restart' (a nil value)\nstack traceback:\n        [string \":lua\"]:1: in main chunk\n\nAPI doesn't take any argument and from this code: \n  \n    \n      mini.nvim/lua/mini/sessions.lua\n    \n    \n         Line 345\n      in\n      69b7433\n    \n  \n  \n    \n\n        \n          \n           MiniSessions.restart = function() \n        \n    \n  \n\n\nlooks like it should work in all situation. If session is loaded it would restart same session, if session is not loaded, it creates temporary session and load it when neovim restarts.\nCan someone please tell me how to use this API?",
