                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "Yep, looks like it. @cosmosb, chances are that current 'mini.nvim' installation uses either `stable` branch or tracks version tags. Available solutions here are: update to track `main` branch or wait for the new release (which will be a while, I am afraid).",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Yep, looks like it. <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/cosmosb/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/cosmosb\">@cosmosb</a>, chances are that current 'mini.nvim' installation uses either <code class=\"notranslate\">stable</code> branch or tracks version tags. Available solutions here are: update to track <code class=\"notranslate\">main</code> branch or wait for the new release (which will be a while, I am afraid).</p>",
                    "bodyText": "Yep, looks like it. @cosmosb, chances are that current 'mini.nvim' installation uses either stable branch or tracks version tags. Available solutions here are: update to track main branch or wait for the new release (which will be a while, I am afraid).",
